      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under nitrogen (drybox/Schlenk), Ce (0.140 g, 1.00 mmol), PhSeSePh (0.468 g, 1.50 mmol) and Hg (0.020 g, 0.10 mmol) were combined in THF (20 mL) and stirred until the metal dissolved (2 days), giving a yellow solution and greenish yellow solid. pySO3 (0.040 g, 0.25 mmol) was added and the flask was refrigerated for 3 days, giving a golden yellow solution and trace black solid. After warming to room temperature the solution was filtered, reduced in volume under vacuum (20 mL) and layered with 12 mL of hexanes to give yellow block crystals (0.117 g, 20%). Low-temperature preparation was used to avoid Se substitution at the sulfide site.",
