        "procedure": "Under nitrogen, Ho (0.165 g, 1.00 mmol), PhTeTePh (0.616 g, 1.50 mmol) and Hg (0.043 g, 0.215 mmol) were combined in pyridine (40 mL) and stirred until the metals dissolved (24 h). Elemental Te (0.255 g, 2.00 mmol) and TeO2 (0.320 g, 2.00 mmol) were added to the dark red-brown solution and stirred for 2 days. The dark red solution with grey-black precipitate was filtered, reduced to ca. 30 mL and layered with 20 mL hexane. Dark red-orange block crystals of the two-cluster co-crystal formed in 1–2 days (0.046 g, 6.7%). The chemistry is light-sensitive.",
